SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Equipment Check | Week 1 DC Lab Kit
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE
  LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned
 /Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• E
 TA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER
  TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event, you shoul
 d be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are re
 quired for the next practical session and what each item is for.\n• Conf
 irm every critical item is ready, compatible, and safe to use before the
  lab begins.\n• Identify any missing item early enough to obtain or subs
 titute it without cancelling the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe a
 ssigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in th
 is outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these
  items after the session, do not count that item as complete. Write the 
 concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or suppleme
 ntal resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish 
 the assigned work, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot
  explain or demonstrate an outcome, write that one concept on a short ca
 tch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. No spr
 eadsheet logging is required.
