SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 01 | START FROM ZERO — Electricity Basics + Sa
 fety + Ohm/Watt — Learn
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nSTART FROM ZERO — SESSION 1\
 nWHY THIS STARTS HERE: Every later embedded-system skill assumes you und
 erstand what voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, ground\, polarity\
 , open circuits\, shorts\, and safe measurement mean. We are not assumin
 g prior electronics knowledge.\n\nWEEK 1 FOCUS: START FROM ZERO: Safety 
 + What Electricity Is + Voltage / Current / Resistance + Ohm / Watt + SI
  Prefixes\nETA/CETa SCOPE — FIRST PASS: 1.1\, 1.4–1.7\, 1.10\, 1.13–1.14
 \; 2.1\, 2.4\, 2.6\, 2.13–2.14\; 9.8–9.9. The narrower RF/fiber/field-sa
 fety details return later in CETa-specific review.\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURP
 OSE: Build the vocabulary and safety habits every later circuit\, instru
 ment\, microcontroller\, and troubleshooting skill depends on. Set up th
 e Git evidence notebook from day one.\n\nTODAY — 8:00 PM TO 9:30 PM:\n1.
  Safety first (10 min): electrical shock basics\, de-energizing\, ESD\, 
 and why resistance measurements are made on de-energized circuits.\n2. W
 hat electricity is (15 min): charge/electrons at a practical technician 
 level\; do not get buried in atomic physics.\n3. Learn voltage vs curren
 t vs resistance vs power (25 min). Explain each in your own words before
  moving on.\n4. Open the ETA Common Formulas sheet and locate Ohm's law 
 / power relationships (5 min).\n5. Work 6–8 beginner Ohm/Watt problems w
 ith units (15 min). Show the rearrangement\; do not copy an example.\n6.
  Set up or confirm the GitHub lab notebook/repository (10 min). Create a
  Week_01 folder/note.\n\nMASTERY GATE: In plain language\, explain charg
 e\, voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, polarity\, open vs short\, 
 and basic ESD/shock precautions\; use SI prefixes\; solve fresh Ohm/Watt
  problems\; then build and safely measure a current-limited LED circuit 
 on Saturday.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Learn from the bottom. Watching alone neve
 r counts. Use learn → retrieve → calculate/code → build/measure → debug 
 → document. Start later study blocks with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. 
 A missed session never creates an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nWEEK 1 
 START-FROM-ZERO RESOURCES:\n• Electric Current and Circuits Explained: h
 ttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r-SCyD7f_zI\n• Electrical Safety Training
 : https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TMT6f3tZQSk\n• GitHub Skills — Introdu
 ction to GitHub: https://github.com/skills/introduction-to-github\n\nREF
 ERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide, 6t
 h ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers i
 n BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTE
 rrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE:
  Ch.1 pp.1–6 SKIM only\; Ch.2 pp.7–14\; Ch.3 pp.16–18\; Ch.4 pp.25–26\; 
 read the book addendum once.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.2 quiz p.15 after the sa
 fety lesson. Use answers p.223 only after finishing.\nWHY: Starts from z
 ero with safety\, units\, Ohm/Watt and the physical meaning of voltage/c
 urrent/resistance before circuit analysis.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition
  book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + cur
 rent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curre
 nt topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the 
 end of this event, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Expl
 ain voltage, current, resistance, power, ground/reference, polarity, ope
 n circuits, and short circuits.\n• Use SI prefixes and engineering notat
 ion correctly for common electronic values.\n• Apply Ohm's law and the W
 att/power relationships to simple DC circuits.\n• Recognize basic electr
 ical hazards and use safe low-voltage measurement habits.\n\nCOVERAGE AU
 DIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every 
 item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate on
 e of these items after the session, do not count that item as complete. 
 Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official o
 r supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RUL
 E\nFinish the assigned work, then check the learning outcomes below. If 
 you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome, write that one concept on 
 a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review blo
 ck. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT30M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Study block starts in 30 minutes
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
