 tt and the physical meaning of voltage/current/resistance before circuit
  analysis.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbo
 ok. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever
  the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUI
 RED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the end of this event, you should be
  able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Solve Ohm's law and power problems w
 ith units and SI prefixes.\n• Predict current, voltage drop, resistance,
  and power before measuring.\n• Explain why current limiting and correct
  meter connections matter.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and
  tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If y
 ou still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the sess
 ion, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short ca
 tch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before 
 closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work, th
 en check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstra
 te an outcome, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repai
 r it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is r
 equired.
