SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 01 | START FROM ZERO — Electricity Basics + Sa
 fety + Ohm/Watt — Hands-On Lab + Weekly Reset
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 1 FOCUS: START FROM ZER
 O: Safety + What Electricity Is + Voltage / Current / Resistance + Ohm /
  Watt + SI Prefixes\nETA/CETa SCOPE — FIRST PASS: 1.1\, 1.4–1.7\, 1.10\,
  1.13–1.14\; 2.1\, 2.4\, 2.6\, 2.13–2.14\; 9.8–9.9. The narrower RF/fibe
 r/field-safety details return later in CETa-specific review.\nCAREER/EMB
 EDDED PURPOSE: Build the vocabulary and safety habits every later circui
 t\, instrument\, microcontroller\, and troubleshooting skill depends on.
  Set up the Git evidence notebook from day one.\n\nTODAY — HANDS-ON:\n1.
  Before power: identify the source voltage\, LED polarity\, resistor val
 ue\, and expected current.\n2. Build a low-voltage current-limited LED c
 ircuit on the breadboard.\n3. Predict readings first\; then measure volt
 age/current/resistance safely with the DMM where appropriate.\n4. Introd
 uce one simple open/wiring fault and use a power → ground → visual → con
 tinuity/voltage sequence to find it.\n5. Photograph the setup and record
  expected vs actual readings.\n6. Save a short Week 1 lab note in GitHub
 : objective\, schematic/sketch\, calculations\, measurements\, fault\, r
 oot cause\, fix\, and result.\n\nMASTERY GATE: In plain language\, expla
 in charge\, voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, polarity\, open vs 
 short\, and basic ESD/shock precautions\; use SI prefixes\; solve fresh 
 Ohm/Watt problems\; then build and safely measure a current-limited LED 
 circuit on Saturday.\n\nFINAL 15-MIN WEEKLY RESET:\n• Career Proof: upda
 te Git lab notebook and any DC measurement/fault evidence you created.\n
 • If Yellow/Red\, write one specific carryover weakness and a repair dat
 e.\n\nWEEK 1 START-FROM-ZERO RESOURCES:\n• Electric Current and Circuits
  Explained: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r-SCyD7f_zI\n• Electrical Sa
 fety Training: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TMT6f3tZQSk\n• GitHub Ski
 lls — Introduction to GitHub: https://github.com/skills/introduction-to-
 github\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET St
 udy Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED p
 age numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.
 org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT
 \nREAD / USE: Ch.1 pp.1–6 SKIM only\; Ch.2 pp.7–14\; Ch.3 pp.16–18\; Ch.
 4 pp.25–26\; read the book addendum once.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.2 quiz p.15
  after the safety lesson. Use answers p.223 only after finishing.\nWHY: 
 Starts from zero with safety\, units\, Ohm/Watt and the physical meaning
  of voltage/current/resistance before circuit analysis.\nSOURCE RULE: Th
 e 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency 
 wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or 
 omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK
  01)\nBy the end of this event, you should be able to explain or demonst
 rate:\n• Explain voltage, current, resistance, power, ground/reference, 
 polarity, open circuits, and short circuits.\n• Use SI prefixes and engi
 neering notation correctly for common electronic values.\n• Apply Ohm's 
 law and the Watt/power relationships to simple DC circuits.\n• Recognize
  basic electrical hazards and use safe low-voltage measurement habits.\n
 • Solve Ohm's law and power problems with units and SI prefixes.\n• Pred
 ict current, voltage drop, resistance, and power before measuring.\n• Ex
 plain why current limiting and correct meter connections matter.\n• Rela
 te calculated voltage/current/power to what a DMM measures on a real cir
 cuit.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inte
 nded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot expla
 in or demonstrate one of these items after the session, do not count tha
 t item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use t
 he linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nW
 EEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for t
 he week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on real h
 ardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\n
 SIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work, then check the learnin
 g outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome, write
  that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next
  available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
