SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 02 | DC Networks + KVL/KCL + Voltage Dividers 
 + DMM — Learn +Map
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 2 FOCUS: DC Networks + 
 KVL/KCL + Voltage Dividers +DMM\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 4.1\; 4.10\; 4.17\; 3.1
 .4\; 8.1–8.4\; 8.16\;9.1–9.2\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Series/parallel n
 etworks\,voltage/current division\, meter range/connection\, LTspice pre
 dictionvs measurement.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Electronic Circuitsp
 laylist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8tSExU1d
 jL6slnjbL\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pd
 f\n- LTspice:https://www.analog.com/en/resources/design-tools-and-calcul
 ators/ltspice-simulator.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Solve unseen series/parall
 el/KVL/KCLproblems\, predict test points\, then verify a built divider n
 etworkwith DMM and explain any measurement error.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ingalone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/m
 easure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 min
 utes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session asjustification for an
  unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy onlythe resources tied to 
 this week’s competencies. Create a one-pagesummary and 5–10 recall promp
 ts. First 10 min: spaced retrieval fromolder material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB 
 — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use 
 your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSI
 GNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.
 pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 p.19 
 series/parallel formulas + Ch.4 pp.27–34.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.4 quiz p.34
 \, then Unit 2 review p.35.\nWHY: The book's DC-circuit sequence aligns 
 directly with series/parallel\, KVL/KCL\, voltage dividers and troublesh
 ooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook.
  Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever th
 e older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED
  LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 02)\nBy the end of this event, you should be ab
 le to explain or demonstrate:\n• Analyze series and parallel resistor ne
 tworks.\n• Use Kirchhoff's Voltage Law and Kirchhoff's Current Law to re
 ason about circuit behavior.\n• Design and analyze a voltage divider, in
 cluding the effect of loading.\n• Predict node voltages, branch currents
 , equivalent resistance, and power.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned reso
 urces and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome l
 ist. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after
  the session, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a
  short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resourc
 e before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned
  work, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or 
 demonstrate an outcome, write that one concept on a short catch-up list 
 and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet log
 ging is required.
