SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 05 | BUFFER 1: DC/AC Fundamentals Mastery Chec
 k — PracticalMastery Gate [GATE]
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 5 FOCUS: BUFFER 1: DC/A
 C Fundamentals MasteryCheck\nETA/CETa SCOPE: Cumulative 1.x\, 2.x\, 4.1–
 4.4/4.10/4.17\, 8.xbasics\, 9.1–9.3/9.7–9.9\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: No
  major new topic.Repair weak fundamentals before adding semiconductor de
 pth.\n\nTHISWEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- ETA CETa competencies:https://www.etai.
 org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Com
 mon_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: ≥80% on a30-question mixed set\; indep
 endently complete onecalculate→simulate→build→measure→fault-isolate circ
 uit\; all missesdocumented.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts
 . Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> do
 cument. Starteach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall
 . Never use amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmar
 athon.\n\nTODAY:\nIndependently calculate\, build\, measure andfault-iso
 late one low-voltage circuit. Stop at 2 hours\; unfinisheditems become n
 ext week’s first task.\n\nFOUNDATION GATE — ADVANCE/REPEAT DECISION: GRE
 EN = mastery is demonstrable and you advance. YELLOW = advance but carry
  no more than 1–2 specific weak items forward with a short written repai
 r date. RED = a core/safety/practical gap is material\; use the next ava
 ilable buffer/repair block before treating the gate as complete. The cal
 endar date never overrides competence.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LIN
 KS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Goo
 gle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6
 th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL 
 STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: No major new chapter. Revi
 sit Ch.2 quiz p.15\, Ch.4 quiz p.34\, Unit 2 review p.35 and formula p.2
 24.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Use the book questions as part of the 30-question mi
 xed check\; repair every miss.\nWHY: This is a mastery/buffer week\, so 
 the book becomes a cumulative retrieval source rather than adding new ma
 terial.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook.
  Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever th
 e older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED
  LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 05)\nBy the end of this event, you should be ab
 le to explain or demonstrate:\n• Integrate Weeks 1-4 without relying on 
 isolated memorized facts.\n• Solve mixed DC/AC, Ohm/Watt, series/paralle
 l, KVL/KCL, divider, waveform, and passive-component problems.\n• Choose
  the correct test instrument and measurement method for a stated problem
 .\n• Build, measure, and fault-isolate a simple circuit independently.\n
 • Document weak areas and repair them before calling the foundation comp
 lete.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inte
 nded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot expla
 in or demonstrate one of these items after the session, do not count tha
 t item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use t
 he linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nS
 IMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work, then check the learning
  outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome, write 
 that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next 
 available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
