 or Works (Engineering Mindset):https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GQatiB-JH
 dI\n\nMASTERY GATE: Identifyunfamiliar passive/relay examples by symbol/
 photo\, state key ratingsand likely failure symptoms\, and drive a relay
 /load safely.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> 
 retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start e
 achnon-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use ami
 ssed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY
 :\nStudy only the resources tied to this week’scompetencies. Create a on
 e-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. First10 min: spaced retrieval fr
 om older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Asso
 ciate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and t
 he PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https
 ://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOO
 K ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.7 pp.53–58 + Unit 3 review pp.59–61 + Ch.8 
 pp.62–69.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.7 quiz p.58 and Ch.8 quiz p.69.\nWHY: Combi
 nes motors/generators with the broad component-recognition knowledge use
 d in lab troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the prim
 ary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata c
 ontrol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTE
 R TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 07)\nBy the end of this event
 , you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Identify common passi
 ve component families, ratings, tolerances, markings, and practical fail
 ure modes.\n• Explain basic magnetic-field, electromagnet, relay, motor,
  generator, and alternator concepts.\n• Distinguish relay coils/contacts
  and understand why inductive loads need suppression.\n• Explain the rol
 e of resistors, capacitors, inductors, transformers, switches, fuses, an
 d relays in real circuits.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and
