SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 07 | Passive Components + Magnetism + Motors/G
 enerators +Relays — Calculate + CETa Questions
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 7 FOCUS: Passive Compon
 ents + Magnetism +Motors/Generators + Relays\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 2.1–2.9\; 
 3.1–3.4.2\;3.9–3.9.3\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Component recognition\, r
 atings\,polarity\, thermistors\, inductors\, transformer cores\, relayco
 ils/contacts and flyback context.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-Electronic
 s for Beginners:https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLzqS33DOPhJkRn6e9
 _OTdQwRojO8qlusI\n- Electricity and Magnetism:https://www.youtube.com/pl
 aylist?list=PLv0qva_0Z5RrBlJkB7w2J8IcFEKZ1YyRq\n- PRIMARY — How a DC Mot
 or Works (Engineering Mindset):https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GQatiB-JH
 dI\n\nMASTERY GATE: Identifyunfamiliar passive/relay examples by symbol/
 photo\, state key ratingsand likely failure symptoms\, and drive a relay
 /load safely.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> 
 retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start e
 achnon-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use ami
 ssed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY
 :\nWork fresh calculations/recognition questionswithout notes. Use the o
 fficial formula sheet when allowed. Target≥80%\; every miss gets an ETA 
 competency number and written correction.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE 
 LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/
 Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ET
 A 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICI
 AL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.7 pp.53–58 + Unit 3 
 review pp.59–61 + Ch.8 pp.62–69.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.7 quiz p.58 and Ch.8
  quiz p.69.\nWHY: Combines motors/generators with the broad component-re
 cognition knowledge used in lab troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-e
 dition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording
  + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a
  current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 07)\nB
 y the end of this event, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n
 • Interpret ratings, tolerance, coil/contact values, and basic electrome
 chanical relationships.\n• Select parts from markings/datasheets and jus
 tify the choice.\n• Use datasheets/markings and measurements to verify a
  component or electromechanical device.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned 
 resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outco
 me list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items a
 fter the session, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept 
 on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental res
 ource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assi
 gned work, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain
  or demonstrate an outcome, write that one concept on a short catch-up l
 ist and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet
  logging is required.
