SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 08 | Semiconductors: Diodes + BJT/FET/MOSFET +
  SCR/TRIAC —Learn + Map
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 8 FOCUS: Semiconductors
 : Diodes + BJT/FET/MOSFET +SCR/TRIAC\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 3.5–3.7.3\nCAREER/
 EMBEDDED PURPOSE:Switching\, biasing\, logic-level MOSFETs\, flyback dio
 des\, Zenerregulation\, semiconductor fault symptoms.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RES
 OURCES:\n-Electronics for Beginners:https://www.youtube.com/playlist?lis
 t=PLzqS33DOPhJkRn6e9_OTdQwRojO8qlusI\n- NMOS vs PMOS / Enhancement vs De
 pletion:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kY-ka0PriaE\n- ETA CETa competen
 cies:https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Identify
 devices and terminals\, analyze simple bias/current/power\, select atran
 sistor/MOSFET as a switch\, and troubleshoot one intentionallymiswired c
 ircuit.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Uselearn -> retrie
 ve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->document. Start each no
 n-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spacedrecall. Never use a missed 
 session as justification for an unhealthymake-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nSt
 udy only the resources tied to thisweek’s competencies. Create a one-pag
 e summary and 5–10 recall prompts.First 10 min: spaced retrieval from ol
 der material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate
  CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PR
 INTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://ww
 w.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASS
 IGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.9 pp.70–78 + Ch.10 pp.79–83.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.
 9 quiz p.78\, Ch.10 quiz p.83 and Unit 4 review p.84.\nWHY: Directly sup
 ports semiconductor recognition\, switching behavior and discrete-device
  troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa
  textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control w
 henever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY 
 — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 08)\nBy the end of this event, you sh
 ould be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain PN junction behavior 
 and the operation/use of rectifier diodes, LEDs, Zener diodes, and prote
 ction diodes.\n• Explain BJT switching at a practical level and distingu
 ish NPN/PNP behavior.\n• Explain FET/MOSFET gate control, source/drain r
 oles, logic-level switching, and common protection concerns.\n• Recogniz
 e SCR/TRIAC purpose and where controlled switching devices are used.\n\n
 COVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to c
 over every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or dem
 onstrate one of these items after the session, do not count that item as
  complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked
  official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COM
 PLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work, then check the learning outcomes
  below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome, write that one 
 concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available
  review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
