 STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.9 pp.70–78 + Ch.10 pp.7
 9–83.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.9 quiz p.78\, Ch.10 quiz p.83 and Unit 4 review
  p.84.\nWHY: Directly supports semiconductor recognition\, switching beh
 avior and discrete-device troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition
  book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + cur
 rent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curre
 nt topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 08)\nBy the 
 end of this event, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Expl
 ain PN junction behavior and the operation/use of rectifier diodes, LEDs
 , Zener diodes, and protection diodes.\n• Explain BJT switching at a pra
 ctical level and distinguish NPN/PNP behavior.\n• Explain FET/MOSFET gat
 e control, source/drain roles, logic-level switching, and common protect
 ion concerns.\n• Recognize SCR/TRIAC purpose and where controlled switch
 ing devices are used.\n• Reason about diode drops, current limiting, tra
 nsistor/MOSFET switching conditions, and device ratings.\n• Recognize wh
 ether a semiconductor device is being used safely within its stated limi
 ts.\n• Select and wire a basic transistor/MOSFET switch with appropriate
  current limiting/flyback protection.\n• Troubleshoot common semiconduct
 or-switching faults with a meter or scope.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assign
 ed resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this ou
 tcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these item
 s after the session, do not count that item as complete. Write the conce
 pt on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental 
 resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practica
 l is the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Green only whe
 n the knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measurements without f
 ollowing a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the 
 assigned work, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot exp
 lain or demonstrate an outcome, write that one concept on a short catch-
 up list and repair it during the next available review block. No spreads
 heet logging is required.
