SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 10 | Amplifiers + Op-Amps + Gain + Loading — H
 ands-On Lab +Mastery
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 10 FOCUS: Amplifiers + 
 Op-Amps + Gain +Loading\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 11.1–11.9\; 9.6\nCAREER/EMBEDDE
 D PURPOSE:Analog signal conditioning for sensors\; gain\, feedback\,satu
 ration/distortion\, bandwidth\, scope/meter loading.\n\nTHIS WEEK'SRESOU
 RCES:\n- Transistor Bias & Amplifier Classes:https://www.youtube.com/wat
 ch?v=c6cmkm3UPUI\n- Op-Amp Circuits:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K03R
 om3Cs28\n- Common-Emitter Gain &Frequency Response: https://www.youtube.
 com/watch?v=NizrzRKQqII\n\nMASTERY GATE: Calculate basic gain\, distingu
 ish amplifier classes and op-amproles\, predict clipping/loading\, and m
 easure an analog stage withoutcorrupting it.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching a
 lone never counts. Use learn-> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measu
 re -> debug -> document.Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes
  of spaced recall. Neveruse a missed session as justification for an unh
 ealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild/measure/debug the practical obj
 ective.Photograph or capture evidence\, document expected vs actual\, an
 dcommit the lab note/code. Completion requires demonstration\, notwatchi
 ng.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study
  Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page
  numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org
 /6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nR
 EAD / USE: Ch.12 pp.91–101.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.12 quiz p.101 + Unit 5 re
 view pp.102–103.\nWHY: Provides the CETa analog-amplifier and dB foundat
 ion\; labs add the practical embedded signal-conditioning angle.\nSOURCE
  RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA co
 mpetency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book di
 ffers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCO
 MES (WEEK 10)\nBy the end of this event, you should be able to explain o
 r demonstrate:\n• Explain voltage gain, current gain, power gain, loadin
 g, input/output impedance, and feedback.\n• Use decibels at a basic tech
 nician level and relate dB changes to gain/loss.\n• Distinguish common a
 mplifier classes and basic transistor/FET amplifier roles.\n• Explain id
 eal op-amp assumptions at an introductory level.\n• Calculate basic volt
 age/power gain and dB relationships.\n• Predict amplifier output limits 
 and identify clipping/loading from numerical or waveform evidence.\n• Re
 cognize inverting, non-inverting, buffer/comparator-style applications a
 nd the role of feedback.\n• Measure or simulate an amplifier and diagnos
 e clipping, bias, loading, or gain problems.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assi
 gned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this 
 outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these it
 ems after the session, do not count that item as complete. Write the con
 cept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplementa
 l resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practi
