 explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain I2C controller/target roles, SDA/SCL,
  addressing, pull-ups, start/stop, read/write, ACK/NACK, and basic trans
 actions.\n• Explain SPI controller/peripheral roles, SCLK, MOSI, MISO, c
 hip select, transaction framing, and the idea of clock mode.\n• Choose I
 2C or SPI appropriately for a simple peripheral and wire it correctly.\n
 • Use a logic analyzer to capture and decode UART and the chosen I2C/SPI
  bus.\n• Integrate a real sensor/peripheral and convert raw data into me
 aningful units.\n• Interface a digital input/output or actuator safely a
 nd verify the end-to-end signal path.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned re
