 ild\, measure\, debug and document the week’sdeliverable. Update Git/pro
 ject evidence. Stop at the scheduled end\; donot compensate for a missed
  session with a marathon.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offici
 al Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive cop
 y and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata
 : https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE —
  V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.13 pp.104–112 + Ch.15 pp.120–130 + C
 h.22 pp.188–193.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.13 quiz p.112\, Ch.15 quiz p.130\, U
 nit 6 review p.131 and Ch.22 quiz p.193.\nWHY: Compresses the low-embedd
 ed-priority RF/telecom material while also learning the documentation be
 havior that matters in real technical jobs.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-editio
 n book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + cu
 rrent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curr
 ent topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 20)\nBy the
  end of this event, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Exp
 lain introductory RF concepts: frequency bands, propagation, modulation,
  transmission lines, antennas, and standing-wave/impedance ideas at CETa
  level.\n• Recognize basic transmitter/receiver and telecom/telephone si
 gnal-path concepts.\n• Understand technician procedures involving docume
 ntation, records, professionalism, and technical communication.\n• Relat
 e RF/telecom symptoms to likely path, connector, configuration, or signa
 l problems.\n• Use the CETa references to recognize terminology without 
 over-studying material that is not central to the bridge-job path.\n• In
 tegrate broad CETa knowledge with the electronics/test foundation alread
 y built.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are i
 ntended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot ex
 plain or demonstrate one of these items after the session, do not count 
 that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and us
 e the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n
