SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 24 | Project 1 Hardware Bring-Up — Lab / Proje
 ct / Mastery
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 24 FOCUS: Project 1 Har
 dware Bring-Up\nETA/CETa SCOPE:Maintenance retrieval only\nCAREER/EMBEDD
 ED PURPOSE: Power\, GPIO\,button\, controlled output\, UART\, clean wiri
 ng\, railmeasurements/current draw.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 M
 CUDeveloper Zone: https://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-develop
 er-zone.html\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas
 .pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Boardpowers safely\, core I/O and UART work\, meas
 urements are documented\,and at least one bring-up failure has a root-ca
 use story.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> ret
 rieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start each
 non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use amisse
 d session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\n
 Build\, measure\, debug and document the week’sdeliverable. Update Git/p
 roject evidence. Stop at the scheduled end\; donot compensate for a miss
 ed session with a marathon.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offi
 cial Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive c
 opy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. erra
 ta: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE
  — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.11 pp.85–90\, Ch.18 pp.1
 59–164 and Ch.19 pp.165–175 during hardware bring-up.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No
  new book quiz\; cite the relevant page in your troubleshooting notes wh
 en it informs a decision.\nWHY: Reuses CETa material as real engineering
 -lab procedure instead of separating certification knowledge from job sk
 ill.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Cu
 rrent ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the o
 lder book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LE
 ARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 24)\nBy the end of this event, you should be able 
 to explain or demonstrate:\n• Perform safe first power-up using visual i
 nspection, continuity checks, a current-limited supply, and measured pow
 er rails.\n• Verify board power, ground, reset/boot conditions, GPIO, an
 d UART before adding complexity.\n• Measure voltage/current and record b
 aseline current draw.\n• Use SWD/UART diagnostics to separate hardware, 
 firmware, and configuration faults.\n• Apply staged bring-up rather than
  powering everything at once.\n• Document bring-up evidence and any faul
 t/recovery story.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks ab
 ove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still 
 cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session, do n
 ot count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up li
 st and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing t
 he gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof
  point for the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be us
 ed on real hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step t
 utorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work, then check
  the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an ou
 tcome, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it dur
 ing the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
