SUMMARY:AU-ESET 301 | Week 26 | Project 1 Firmware Architecture — Learn /
  Retrieve
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\nWEEK 26 FOCUS: Project 1 Fir
 mware Architecture\nETA/CETaSCOPE: 13.10–13.12 spaced review\nCAREER/EMB
 EDDED PURPOSE: Timers\,interrupts\, PWM\, nonblocking FSM\, timeouts\, e
 rror codes anddiagnostic output.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU 
 DeveloperZone: https://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-
 zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Firmware runs without long blocking delays\, 
 timing ismeasured\, error paths are exercised\, and architecture can be 
 explainedat interview depth.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never count
 s. Uselearn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->do
 cument. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spacedrecall
 . Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthymake-up ma
 rathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from priorweeks. Study th
 is week’s scoped material and make a one-page memorysummary. Complete 8–
 12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content applies.School work takes prior
 ity during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Off
 icial Associate CET Study Guide, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive 
 copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. err
 ata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUID
 E — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.17 pp.151–155 and Ch.16
  logic/sequential sections pp.136–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Explain your firm
 ware state machine and hardware-control flow without the book open.\nWHY
 : Connects book control/programming concepts to structured embedded firm
 ware.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. C
 urrent ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the 
 older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED L
 EARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 26)\nBy the end of this event, you should be able
  to explain or demonstrate:\n• Organize Project 1 firmware into understa
 ndable modules with clear responsibilities.\n• Use a nonblocking finite-
 state machine for system behavior.\n• Use timers/interrupts where approp
 riate without creating timing-dependent chaos.\n• Implement timeouts, er
 ror states, diagnostic messages, and recoverable fault handling.\n\nCOVE
 RAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover
  every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonst
 rate one of these items after the session, do not count that item as com
 plete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked off
 icial or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLET
 ION RULE\nFinish the assigned work, then check the learning outcomes bel
 ow. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome, write that one conc
 ept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available rev
 iew block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
